The taller card text required more vertical room: network height is now `min(780px, calc(100svh - clamp(96px, 13.5vh, 180px)))`; desktop summaries hide on screens ≤860 px high, alongside the existing width-based fallback. This prevents the card rows from colliding while retaining the approved layout.

Verified at 1440 × 900: heading 48.96 px, body 23.04 px, project names 21.6 px, labels 16 px, and a 27 px gap between card rows. The two-line heading is retained. Checks at 1024 × 768, 900 × 600, and a fresh-load 1280 × 800 showed cards fitting their viewport. Work → Cases still covers its target slot; reverse returns to Work with cards visible and then to Hero. TypeScript passed, and a clean browser reload had no console errors. When checking changed breakpoints, load a fresh route rather than relying on a hash left at a previous viewport's scroll position.

