### 8. Adaptive repeated input and navigation cancellation

- Existing gesture ownership now recognizes deliberate repeats, accelerates the
  active local timeline to 3×, and retains one latest directional request for a
  safe asynchronous handoff. Tiny sign changes in trackpad tails do not reverse
  the story; modified/editing/native activation input retains browser behavior.
- Hero includes Work's local entrance in its owned timeline. Restoration seeks
  Work to its readable rest; chapter/closing controllers are retained and killed
  on cancellation. Footer and home glides hurry without restarting their journey.
- Direct navigation cancels older requests/controllers, including a pending step
  at the same target. Held keys remain usable in the released native footer.
- Added `scripts/handoff-input-check.cjs` and `scripts/adaptive-input-check.js`.
  TypeScript, build, input assertions, production interaction/regression checks,
  reduced motion and native-touch emulation passed; measurements appear above.

### 9. Single-scroll grouping and restrained wheel pacing

- Reproduced and fixed a real gap in the previous tests: decaying momentum with
  80ms pauses was mistaken for repeated commands and crossed two boundaries.
- Wheel repeats now hurry only the current move at 1.8×; they do not queue another
  forward section. Grouping uses 240ms quiet plus decay detection below 700ms idle,
  preserving meaningful direction through noisy tails. Keys/navigation remain
  explicit fast controls, and cancellation/reverse cleanup are preserved.
- Added `scripts/single-scroll-check.js`, expanded input assertions to 21 groups,
  and updated the adaptive regression to require one wheel boundary. Production
  build, replayed single-scroll traces, repeat controls, reverse/replay, shared
  preview geometry and responsive checks passed. Current evidence appears above.

